Z||000000||cardealer||04-18-2001||11:33 AM||||i am changing my electric water pump to a high volume belt drive and i understand that i have to mount it upside down, do i plug the little water hole on the block and the hole into the water pump return outlet? and if i need to plug it what do i use? i realize this sounds confusing, but any one that has ever had to mount their w.p. up side down will know what i am talking about.<BR>thanks!  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||04-18-2001||11:49 AM||||whats wrong with the electric unit??? CSI , moroso  , other??<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000002||cardealer||04-18-2001||12:10 PM||||i live in texas and already had a couple of days of 80 degree weather, although it hasnt overheated yet, as hard as i drive i dont think it will hold upto 100 degree weather.<BR>i am using a weiand pump now and it just dosnt push the water through my 5 core well enough.<BR> a second question (now that i think about it) is anyone (living in a hot climate) using a mr. gasket electric water pump drive kit with the larger pulley and longer belt? this is supposed to increase the flow as much as 40%. i am wondering if this along with a high flow waterpump would be enough to cool during hot days? i really dont mind cutting a hole in my wheelwell for the belt, but if i dont have to... all the better!<BR>thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Archie||04-18-2001||01:59 PM||||Yes, you will need to plug that hole on both the pump & the engine block.<P>Do you still have your Video Instruction tape?.... It tells you how to plug it.<P>Anyway you'll find that the cast hole in these 2 areas is 3/8" Dia. now. So you can Tap them using a 7/16-14 Tap. about 8 to 10 threads deep. Then use a 7/16"-14 bolt and some sealer and tighten the bolt into the holes and cut it off.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||cardealer||04-18-2001||02:35 PM||||thanks archie, i am sorry i dont have your video tape. i did my own kit thing this time. somedays i wish i would have just purchased your kit, but everything worked out doing it myself suprisingly well. if there is a next time... i am purchasing your kit!<BR>thanks again!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||04-18-2001||03:34 PM||||CARDDEALER- If you need the tape I'll send it to you.  It's sitting around my buddies shop somewhere.  No offense meant Archie but that tape has some hilarious scenes in it.  Especially the one where you're talking about getting something into position with a little tapping with a hammer or something like that and you disappear back under the tranny or engine and then you hear this loud banging (and some cussing I think) and then you reappear and continue with the instruction as if nothing unusual has happened.  It's entertaining.  ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Butter||04-19-2001||11:54 AM||||Cardealer,<BR>With Archie's radiator and a CSI electric pump I have had no trouble overheating in 95+ degree temps.  The CSI pump does require a hole in the fender well though.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jimmy||04-19-2001||11:41 PM||||Hey Butter, thanks for the waterpump pics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I think I may design some sort of cover that will cover the hole.  Shouldn't be too dificult.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000008||Butter||04-20-2001||09:54 AM||||Jimmy,<BR>I'd like to see the cover if you get around to building it.  I wanted to do this myself but you know how those things can go.  By the way, I had an unfortunate accident Monday when I separated the right rear tire from the rim.  The tire did not get into the pump at all with no cover.  I was surprised.||||reg||1
